(text "R1 and both cut ends of W1's red wire go into U1's 2-way\nscrew terminal: VIN+ = laptop end + R1 leg, VIN- = Nano end +\nother R1 leg. The current never crosses the breadboard." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 248.92 15.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "1be46563-f92e-5ddf-8028-fbb526a35a30"))
(text "INA219: VIN+ = laptop side, VIN- = Nano side (high side).\nBus voltage is read at VIN- = the Nano's VBUS, so P = V x I is\nthe power delivered to the Nano. VCC from the ESP32 3V3, never\nfrom the Nano. Module keeps its 10k I2C pull-ups; A0 = A1 = GND.\nShunt option A: R1 = 1 ohm and DESOLDER the module's R100.\nOption B (no soldering): omit R1, keep R100, logger 0.100 ohm." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 210.82 81.28 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b4a29f95-780d-5b11-8c32-a41c4c6574d9"))
