(text "A1 is powered ONLY through its micro-USB (W2), so every joule it uses passes R1.\nPins 17 (3V3), 27 (+5V/VUSB) and 30 (VIN) stay unconnected: anything on them would\nbypass the shunt or load the measured rail. Do not bridge the Nano's VUSB jumper.\nWire A1 pin 4 or 29 (GND) to the breadboard GND rail: that ties the grounds." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 152.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e79704d2-4472-5c72-9cfc-72ca9ce9cc41"))
(text "D2 = sync output of firmware/bench: LOW at rest, HIGH only around measured loops.\nR7 100k + GPIO4 INPUT_PULLDOWN hold SYNC LOW while D2 floats (reset, upload).\nNo push button: the SYNC row's source is one dupont wire. Normal = from R6 (JP4 1-2).\nCalibration = Nano unplugged, move that wire end to the 3V3 rail for >= 10 s, then\npull it out (JP4 2-3). Never put the wire on 3V3 while the Nano's D2 is also wired:\nremove the D2-R6 wire first. The logger ignores bounces shorter than 100 ms." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 166.37 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e036fe2c-1cc6-55fb-a315-88c4ca79bdbb"))
