(text "U2 sits off the breadboard (too wide): use\nfemale-male dupont wires from its pins:\n3V3 -> + rail, GND -> - rail, IO21 -> SDA,\nIO22 -> SCL, IO4 -> SYNC row.\n\nPowered from laptop USB port 2 (its own\nmicro-USB). VIN (pin 15) stays unconnected:\nnever feed the logger from the measured rail." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 208.28 116.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "0244618c-f6bf-5682-82c5-78ebaf51d587"))
(text "logger.ino pin map (CONTRACT 7.3):\n IO21 = SDA, IO22 = SCL, 400 kHz\n IO4  = SYNC, INPUT_PULLDOWN, ISR on CHANGE\n INA219 at 0x40, 12-bit, PGA /1 (+-40 mV),\n   BRNG 16 V, about 1 kHz shunt+bus pairs\n W line within 500 ms of each D2 fall (7.4)\n\nBuild with the measured shunt:\n arduino-cli compile --fqbn esp32:esp32:esp32\n  --build-property \"compiler.cpp.extra_flags=\n  -DSHUNT_OHM_MEASURED=1.012\" logger" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 340.36 119.38 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6a08b888-bb69-5cc2-b1e2-aa362740043f"))
(polyline (pts (xy 11.43 195.58) (xy 294.64 195.58)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type dash)) (uuid "4843ac87-42de-5d18-a466-c2e30f4a3a40"))
(polyline (pts (xy 294.64 195.58) (xy 294.64 284.48)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type dash)) (uuid "5217c24b-b689-527b-b6d4-0d6b4a0ec5d8"))
(polyline (pts (xy 294.64 284.48) (xy 11.43 284.48)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type dash)) (uuid "51e39f49-27b5-5600-9d5e-1780546dc2a2"))
(polyline (pts (xy 11.43 284.48) (xy 11.43 195.58)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type dash)) (uuid "c76c3da7-f6c7-5efa-82a7-1f21417e8c67"))
(text "BUILD NOTES (breadboard, parts on hand: Nano 33 BLE, INA219, ESP32, 1R / 100R / 1k / 100k)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 196.85 0) (effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left top)) (uuid "7d56a624-de75-5992-85a2-72ed2945552e"))
(text "1. Measured path: laptop port 1 -> W1 (USB-A M/F extension, only the red VBUS wire cut) -> U1 VIN+ terminal -> R1 -> U1 VIN- terminal\n   -> W1 -> W2 -> Nano. USB data never leaves the cable, so enumeration and the 115200-baud CDC link are unaffected.\n2. Shunt option A (default; matches logger.ino SHUNT_OHM_MEASURED = 1.000): R1 = your 1 ohm, clamped in U1's screw terminal,\n   and DESOLDER the module's own R100 (0.1 ohm). If R100 stays, the shunt is 0.091 ohm and every energy is 11x off.\n   Range with PGA /1 (+-40 mV): 0 to 40 mA; the Nano needs about 11 mA (vrig assumption), so R1 drops about 11 mV.\n   Option B (no soldering iron): leave R1 out, keep R100, build the logger with the DMM value (about 0.100); range 0-400 mA.\n3. Measure the shunt with a DMM every session -> session_log.csv shunt_ohm_measured and -DSHUNT_OHM_MEASURED.\n   Measure across the screw-terminal screws, Nano unplugged (subtract the DMM lead resistance).\n4. Grounds: one breadboard GND rail joins Nano GND (A1 pin 4 or 29), INA219 GND and ESP32 GND. Ground current does not\n   affect a high-side shunt. 3V3 rail: fed only by the ESP32 3V3 pin; feeds INA219 VCC and the manual sync wire.\n5. I2C: INA219 SDA/SCL rows -> ESP32 IO21/IO22 with wires <= 20 cm. The module's 10k pull-ups are enough at that length.\n6. Sync: A1 D2 -> R6 100R -> SYNC row -> ESP32 IO4, R7 100k from the SYNC row to GND. R6 limits current if only one board\n   is powered. D2 HIGH draws about 0.1 mA from the Nano, in IDLE and RUN windows alike, so it cancels in dE.\n7. Calibration with one load (1k, 5.0 mA) checks offset (open) and gain at one point. A 470R and a 220R (10.6 / 22.7 mA,\n   0.25 W ok) would add linearity points; your 100R would draw 50 mA, beyond the 40 mA range, so it is used for R6.\n8. Not fitted for lack of parts (add later if needed): INA219 input RC filter, extra 4k7 I2C pull-ups, local 100 nF\n   (the module already has one), push button (replaced by the sync wire).\n9. Bring-up order: ESP32 alone (W lines from the sync wire) -> 1k calibration -> Nano with bench firmware (PING, LAT)\n   -> python tools/measure.py --dry-run -> first real session." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 12.7 201.93 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e1dcd402-d205-5603-8236-69aa687b211b"))
(polyline (pts (xy 299.72 198.12) (xy 406.4 198.12)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type dash)) (uuid "99ce17f3-01e0-5ad8-b5c9-5a3f3090cd32"))
(polyline (pts (xy 406.4 198.12) (xy 406.4 251.46)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type dash)) (uuid "17a8fc9b-0574-5517-a10a-70efa6dd0ef5"))
(polyline (pts (xy 406.4 251.46) (xy 299.72 251.46)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type dash)) (uuid "6863a449-32b4-5983-9d7e-0e157fb0b7f9"))
(polyline (pts (xy 299.72 251.46) (xy 299.72 198.12)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type dash)) (uuid "208b16f4-75c2-5bb6-8eb0-0bfdd712c263"))
(text "REQUIREMENT -> WHERE" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 300.99 199.39 0) (effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left top)) (uuid "59a0786b-7457-52a2-9f3a-f3836c02d0c3"))
(text "CONTRACT 7.3 sync on GPIO4, INPUT_PULLDOWN + 100k  -> U2 IO4, R7\nCONTRACT 7.3 INA219 SDA 21 / SCL 22, 400 kHz        -> U2 IO21/IO22\nCONTRACT 7.3 Nano, ESP32, INA219 grounds tied       -> GND rail\nCONTRACT 7.3 D2 push-pull, LOW at rest, floats in reset -> R7, JP4\nCONTRACT 7.4 / logger.ino: INA219 on Nano 5 V USB,  -> R1, U1\n   VIN+ PC side, VIN- Nano side                        (VIN+/VIN-)\nlogger.ino INA219_ADDR 0x40                         -> U1 A0/A1 open\nlogger.ino SHUNT_OHM_MEASURED = 1.000               -> R1 1 ohm\nSprint 2 plan, gate M3: validate on resistor loads  -> R9 1k, JP4 2-3\nmeasure.py --port ttyACM0 / --logger ttyUSB0        -> H1 ports 1/2\nsession_log.csv shunt_ohm_measured                  -> note 3" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 302.26 204.47 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "089952de-e795-568d-9b47-baa8b0da410a"))
(sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
)
